            "notes_base": "Rating 4.3 on Gaode Maps. Opens 09:30-22:00. Located literally next to Huayan Temple (华严寺) on Fanggu Street — arrive for lunch right after stepping off the train and checking in, or after first afternoon sightseeing. Datong-style daoxiaomian (knife-cut noodles) is the city's most iconic dish: noodles hand-shaved from a dough block directly into boiling water, producing thick chewy strips with a characteristic ridged shape. A genuine local gem, not a tourist trap. CNY 21/person.",
            "notes_local": "高德评分4.3，09:30-22:00营业。位于大同仿古街华严寺旁，下火车放好行李后或下午游览完华严寺后直接步行到此。大同刀削面是城市最具代表性的面食：厨师手持刀从面团上直接刮削入沸水，面条厚实筋道带弧度。本地人常去，非景区套餐，人均21元。",
